pam-certauth (0.3.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Catch debian/changelog up with the workspace versions shipped in 0.3.2
    and 0.3.3 (PR #11, #12). Earlier releases shipped a .deb whose
    Version field said 0.3.1-1 even though the binaries were built from
    0.3.2/0.3.3 source — apt refused to upgrade because dpkg saw no
    version increase. This release fixes the metadata and tags 0.3.4.
  * 0.3.2 — USB partitioned-flash support: when the whole-device has no
    filesystem, pam_certauth enumerates partitions and accepts those
    whose ID_FS_TYPE is in the allowlist.
  * 0.3.3 — drop the LABEL=PAMCERT requirement; iterate all USB
    partitions with allowed FS until a .p12 is found. New config
    `max_usb_partitions` (default 8, anti-DoS). Fix:
    `pkcs12_path_pattern` is now honoured by discovery instead of being
    silently ignored; semantics changed to "relative path from mount",
    `${user}` placeholder supported, path-traversal rejected by the
    validator. Default remains `certs/user.p12`.
  * CI: new guardrail step that fails the build if Cargo workspace
    version and debian/changelog top entry disagree (prevents recurrence
    of the metadata mismatch above).

 -- Mikhail Korolev <mikhail@robonet.me>  Sat, 04 Apr 2026 11:20:00 +0300

pam-certauth (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: relax runtime dependencies so the package installs on
    Astra hosts and minimal Debian/Ubuntu deployments out of the box.
    - libgost-engine moved from Depends to Recommends with the Astra
      alternative: `libgost-engine | gost-engine | libgost-astra`. The
      GOST engine is loaded lazily and only when the verified cert
      chain contains GOST-signed certs, so pure RSA deployments no
      longer fail to install.
    - libudev1, libdbus-1-3, libsystemd0 dropped from the explicit
      Depends list — they are populated automatically by
      ${shlibs:Depends} from the binary's NEEDED entries.
    - polkitd | policykit-1 moved from Depends to Suggests; the PAM
      module and daemon do not invoke pkexec today.
    - Mandatory Depends are now limited to libpam0g, lsb-base and
      adduser (plus shlibs/misc substvars).

 -- Mikhail Korolev <mikhail@robonet.me>  Wed, 11 Mar 2026 21:20:00 +0300

pam-certauth (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * MAC integrity (МКЦ): new `[mac]` config section, `pam_cert_max_integrity`
    X.509 extension (OID 2.25.273824307386008814506455310913083078403),
    libpdp FFI binding under the `astra-mac` cargo feature. Orchestrator
    intersects cert max integrity with the user's МНКЦ and applies the
    resulting label to the session via fd-based labeling, closing the
    path-based TOCTOU window. Verified end-to-end on Astra Linux SE 1.8.4
    strict-mode kernel.
  * Strip: removed M-of-N approval, scope policies, and the `execute`
    subcommand path that shipped in 0.2.x. The remaining surface is base
    USB+X.509 PAM auth plus MAC integrity labelling.
  * FFI fixes: libpdp text grammar corrected to "level:ilevel:cat[:flags]",
    dropped `irelax` flag on `pdp_set_fd` (kernel rejects it through the
    fd-based API), link against `libparsec-mic` for `getmicnam`,
    `getmicnam` no longer free'd via `freemicent_r` — per man page the
    returned pointer is library-private static memory; the bogus free
    previously caused `free(): invalid pointer` SIGABRT in
    `pam_sm_open_session`.
  * Daemon: session registry moved from /var/lib/pam_certauth/sessions.json
    to /run/pam_certauth/sessions.json (tmpfs, volatile across reboot).
    Removes stale-state-after-reboot foot-gun and MAC-labelling churn.
    postinst removes the stale /var/lib file on upgrade; daemon.lock and
    caches stay in /var/lib.
  * postinst: raises ilevel=63 on /etc/pam_certauth/config.toml, ca/,
    crl/, host_acl.toml[.sig] when Astra strict mode is enabled (no-op
    on non-Astra / non-strict). Prints opt-in МКЦ activation notice.
  * МКЦ activation: shipped drop-in (mac-integrity.conf.example) now
    uses `PAMName=pam-certauth` with a paired session PAM stack
    (`pam-certauth.example` shipped to /usr/share/pam-certauth/pam.d/)
    that loads pam_parsec_cap.so + pam_parsec_mac.so. Replaces the
    earlier execaps-wrapper approach which failed under
    User=pamcertauth (no PARSEC_CAP_CAP → EPERM in execaps).

 -- Mikhail Korolev <mikhail@robonet.me>  Sun, 22 Feb 2026 14:10:00 +0300

pam-certauth (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: RFC 3161 TimeStampToken is now actually enforced when
    scope policy sets `require_timestamp_token = true` (was a silent
    no-op in 0.2.0). Both chain validation against the [tsa_trust]
    store and RFC 3161 §2.4.1 messageImprint binding to the signer's
    signature octets are checked (SHA-256/384/512).
  * Fix(cms): argv_pattern is now read from the signed
    encapContentInfo.eContent (breaking) rather than the
    tamper-vulnerable sidecar; re-issue work orders with
    `openssl cms -sign -nodetach`.
  * Fix(cms): signing-time is paired with each signer by
    SubjectKeyIdentifier / issuerAndSerialNumber rather than by
    positional index.
  * Fix(packaging): postinst enables pam-certauth-gc.timer and sets
    0750 root:root on /var/lib/pam_certauth/work_orders/.
  * Fix(misc): hooks docstring path corrected; scope-match dedup
    stable; fail-closed host_id_hash; monitord runs non-root cleanly.

 -- Mikhail Korolev <mikhail@robonet.me>  Sat, 07 Feb 2026 12:45:00 +0300

pam-certauth (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(x509): new `pam_cert_scopes` v3 extension. Certificates now
    declare an explicit list of scopes (e.g. `bios.flash`,
    `cluster.drain`). The PAM module gains a `require_scope=...`
    parameter with `scope_match=any|all` to fail login unless the
    cert's scopes satisfy the configured set.
  * feat(execute): new `pam-certauth execute --scope=… --work-order=…
    -- <cmd>` subcommand performs per-action M-of-N authorisation
    against a CMS SignedData work order. Each signer must hold an
    approver cert (separate trust anchor `[approver_trust]`) with
    matching `pam_cert_scopes` and `pam_cert_host_binding`.
  * feat(policy): new `pam_certauth_policy` crate + TOML schema at
    `/etc/pam_certauth/policy.toml`. Scope rules declare `m_of_n`,
    `require_argv_pattern`, `pre_hooks`, `audit_level`. CLI helpers:
    `pam-certauth policy validate`, `pam-certauth policy explain`.
  * feat(retention): CMS work-order artefacts are retained under
    `/var/lib/pam_certauth/work_orders/` for forensic review.
    `pam-certauth gc --retention-days=N` plus systemd timer
    `pam-certauth-gc.timer` reap older entries.
  * feat(audit): every audit event carries `policy_sha256` so a
    sysadmin can detect post-deploy drift of `policy.toml`. Events
    flow via structured journald fields with strict sanitisation.
  * feat(hooks): hooks become a static enum keyed by name with one
    bundled builtin (`audit_critical`). No more arbitrary
    fork+execve from policy.
  * refactor(cli): `pam-certauth-monitord` is gone — the binary is
    now `/usr/bin/pam-certauth` with subcommands `daemon`,
    `execute`, `policy`, `gc`. systemd unit is `pam-certauth.service`
    `ExecStart=/usr/bin/pam-certauth daemon`.
  * refactor(ipc): IPC protocol bumped 1 → 2. `SessionOpen` carries
    `engineer_ski`, `engineer_cert_sha256`, `scopes`, `uid`. New
    message `GetActiveSessionByUid` lets `execute` look up an
    authenticated session by uid. v1 payloads still parse.
  * refactor(config): new sections `[approver_trust]`, `[tsa_trust]`,
    `[policy]`. Old configs still parse. See
    `docs/migration.md` for upgrade.

 -- Mikhail Korolev <mikhail@robonet.me>  Sat, 07 Feb 2026 12:30:00 +0300

pam-certauth (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(pam): wire syslog backend for tracing subscriber. Auth-flow
    errors now land in /var/log/auth.log under syslog ident
    "pam_certauth" (LOG_AUTH facility). Production diagnosis no longer
    blind.
  * fix(pam): cert-binding X.509 extensions take precedence over
    [[user_mapping]]. pam_cert_user_binding / pam_cert_host_binding
    are the sole source of authorisation when present; the TOML
    mapping list is a legacy fallback for certs without the
    user_binding extension.
  * feat(deb): ship SysV init script (/etc/init.d/pam-certauth-monitord)
    via dh_installinit so non-systemd hosts are supported. Adds
    lsb-base dependency.
  * feat(deb): ship man(8) for pam-certauth-monitord.
  * feat(deb): three PAM-stack snippets (certauth / certauth-optional /
    certauth-only) and integrate-pam.sh --mode=2fa|optional|cert-only.
    Cert-only mode bypasses password chain entirely (lockout-strict).
  * docs: USBGuard / Astra ЗПС interop, USB-lockout pre-deploy
    checklist, on_usb_removed mode reference, three operational auth
    modes.
  * test: add leaf_no_user_binding fixture + un-ignore the legacy
    [[user_mapping]] regression test.
  * security: pam-certauth-monitord no longer runs as root. A dedicated
    `pamcertauth` system user is created in postinst; the systemd unit
    runs under this user with CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH only. Privileged
    logind methods (LockSession, TerminateSession, PowerOff) are gated
    by an explicit polkit allowlist shipped at
    /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/49-pam-certauth.rules. Adds adduser and
    polkitd to package Depends. pam_certauth.so itself still runs in
    PAM-caller context (root for sudo/login) — that is an architectural
    constraint of Linux PAM and outside this change.

 -- Mikhail Korolev <mikhail@robonet.me>  Sun, 25 Jan 2026 13:15:00 +0300

